https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-05T16:02:36Z","updated_at":"2021-11-05T16:02:36Z","body":"here is the fix.  this needs a test in test/sql/test_metadata.py if you want to provide a gerrit.  i have it here taking the new value of implicit returning and using it directly, whether it's True or False, overwriting the previous value. the test should exercise that too.   look in test_metadata.py for other tests that are exercising the implicit_returning flag, there are a bunch.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/schema.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/schema.py\r\nindex e45e22564d..14346cf609 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/schema.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/schema.py\r\n@@ -756,6 +756,10 @@ class Table(DialectKWArgs, SchemaItem, TableClause):\r\n         kwargs.pop(\"extend_existing\", False)\r\n         kwargs.pop(\"keep_existing\", False)\r\n \r\n+        self.implicit_returning = kwargs.pop(\r\n+            \"implicit_returning\", self.implicit_returning\r\n+        )\r\n+\r\n         if schema and schema != self.schema:\r\n             raise exc.ArgumentError(\r\n                 \"Can't change schema of existing table from '%s' to '%s'\",\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/962017833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"